@startuml "Adapter - Electricity - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Adapter — a Turkish appliance on an American socket


interface Appliance <<Client-facing>> {
  + setPowerSource(s : TurkishPowerSource)
  + start()
  + stop()
}

interface TurkishPowerSource <<Target>> {
  + providePowerAt220V()
  + turnOn()
  + turnOff()
}

interface USPowerSource <<Adaptee>> {
  + providePowerAt110V()
  + pushSwitch()
}

class TurkishHomeAppliance
class USTurkishPowerAdapter <<Adapter>> {
  - usPowerSource : USPowerSource
  - on : boolean
}

Appliance <|.. TurkishHomeAppliance
TurkishHomeAppliance --> TurkishPowerSource
TurkishPowerSource <|.. USTurkishPowerAdapter
USTurkishPowerAdapter o--> "1" USPowerSource

note right of USTurkishPowerAdapter
  Two operations onto <b>one toggle</b>.
  Only correct if the adapter
  remembers the state — otherwise
  "on" twice leaves it off.
end note

note bottom of TurkishHomeAppliance
  <b>Unchanged and unaware.</b> It holds
  the Target interface, exactly as
  it always did.
end note

@enduml
